[38;5;231m⏺[39m Fixed: [38;5;153msrc/textkit/chunking.py:18[39m.

  [1mRoot cause:[0m the slice was [38;5;153mtext[i:i + chunk_size - 1][39m. Python slice ends are exclusive, so subtracting 1 dropped the
  last character of every chunk — [38;5;153mchunk_text("abcdef", 2)[39m returned [38;5;153m['a', 'c', 'e'][39m, and [38;5;153mchunk_size=1[39m would have returned
  all empty strings. The stride in [38;5;153mrange(0, len(text), chunk_size)[39m was already correct, which is why the tail and
  empty-input cases still looked right.

  [1mFix:[0m [38;5;153mtext[i:i + chunk_size][39m.

